TI Unsupervised clustering of EIS spectra for distinguishing degradation states of polymer coatings
SO PROGRESS IN ORGANIC COATINGS
LA English
DT Article
AB Electrochemical impedance spectra (EIS) from 38 weathered industrial coating systems were analyzed using a fully data-driven, unsupervised machine learning (ML) pipeline to reveal coating degradation patterns, water uptake sensitivity, and to cluster the coatings by barrier integrity. The study systematically compared 30 pipeline configurations comprising normalization, dimensional reduction, and cluster number to identify the feature space for pattern discovery and clustering. The best-performing configuration, per-block normalization of log |Z| and phase combined with three-component principal component analysis (PCA), with t-distributed stochastic neighbor embedding (t-SNE) used for visualization, produced a linear trajectory terminating in the region of the carbon steel (CS) spectra. Most importantly, the unsupervised analysis revealed a medium-frequency (similar to 1 Hz) phase maximum embedded in the non-curated, real-life, coated-sample EIS dataset, aligned with the time constant of the independently measured carbon steel spectra, confirming that the observed trajectory represents a genuine degradation pattern driven by loss of coating integrity and the emergence of the substrate response. Across the coatings tested, hierarchical clustering primarily resolves two degradation-related log |Z| groups, corresponding to coating-dominated (10.746 +/- 0.712) and substrate-influenced (7.453 +/- 1.024) responses. Finer, but less robust, clustering further distinguishes among carbon steel (4.457 +/- 0.012) and, based on analogy with literature classifications, to "poor" (5.705 +/- 0.487), "intermediate" (7.548 +/- 0.616), and "good" (10.381 +/- 0.760) barrier performance states. The applied framework demonstrates that it can act as a sophisticated, fully unsupervised clustering tool by which coating degradation state can be identified automatically and in an unbiased manner.
